# R1.6 behaviour-table probe: multiply (int-preserving, LOSS; scalar arm mirrors *, (A))
define nt(x) as:
    try:
        return num_type of x
    catch e:
        return e.kind
r is multiply of [3037000499, 3037000499]
print of [r, nt of r]
try:
    print of (multiply of [4611686018427387904, 2])
catch e:
    print of ["overflow", e.kind]
l is multiply of [[3, 3037000499], [2, 3037000499]]
print of [l, nt of l[0], nt of l[1]]
